.TH "OPUSSEND" "1" "October 23, 2026" "ka9q-radio" "ka9q-radio Manual"
.SH NAME
opussend \- send local audio as Opus over RTP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B opussend
.RI "[options] -R destination"
.SH STATUS
.B Not actively maintained
.SH DESCRIPTION
opussend captures two-channel audio at 48000 sample frames per second through
PortAudio and transmits RTP/UDP packets. It does not read an RTP input stream
or standard input. Audio is encoded as Opus.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-I device"
Select capture device by exact PortAudio name or numeric index. Use -L to list
devices. An explicit input-capable device is recommended.
.TP
.B "\-R destination"
Set RTP destination. Required for normal operation; default port 5004.
.TP
.B "\-L"
List PortAudio devices and exit.
.TP
.B "\-o bitrate"
Set Opus bitrate. Values below 6000 are interpreted as kbit/s; larger values
are bit/s. Default 32 kbit/s; values above 510000 bit/s are capped.
.TP
.B "\-B milliseconds"
Set Opus frame duration. Default 20 ms. Accepted values are 2.5, 5, 10, 20,
40, 60, 80, 100, and 120; longer durations require supporting libopus
versions.
.TP
.B "\-x"
Enable Opus discontinuous transmission.
.TP
.B "\-f percent"
Enable Opus in-band FEC with the specified expected packet-loss percentage.
.TP
.B "\-p value"
Set IP type-of-service value, parsed with C-style numeric prefixes. Default
48.
.TP
.B "\-T hops"
Set multicast TTL. Default 10.
.TP
.B "\-v"
Increase verbosity.
.TP
.B "\-V"
Print version and exit.
.SH LIMITATIONS
This is an older sender and does not generate the channel metadata used by
current ka9q-radio consumers. Verify compatibility with the intended receiver.
.SH EXAMPLES
List devices and send from capture device 2:
.PP
.nf
opussend \-L
opussend \-I 2 \-R 239.1.2.3:5004
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
monitor(1), pcmrecord(1), radiod(8)
.PP
Project documentation: https://github.com/ka9q/ka9q-radio
